  :adr/id "adr-2800005200-kotoba-library-publication-surfaces"
  :adr/title "Kotoba library publication is CLI-first; language, control, and storage surfaces stay separate"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-08-29"
  :adr/related ["kotoba-lang/kotoba docs/ADR-kotoba-library-publish-cli.md"
                "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang docs/adr/ADR-library-catalog-publication-boundary.md"
                "kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud docs/adr/0001-kotoba-cloud-control-plane.md"]
  :adr/body "# Kotoba library publication surfaces\n\n## Decision\n\nLibrary publication begins in `kotoba library`, not in a second web registry. `kotoba library inspect` exposes the definition CID, release-head CID, exact dependency CID edges, names, and optional GitHub provenance without collapsing those identities. `kotoba library publish` is a dry-run by default; explicit apply reuses the existing signed namespace-head and IPNS publication operation.\n\nThe public surfaces have distinct jobs:\n\n- `kotoba-lang.org/libraries/` is the language-owned catalog and comparison surface. It explains supported libraries, exact dependencies, content-addressed identities, provenance, and comparison axes.\n- `kotoba.cloud` is the account, authorization, deploy, and publication-control surface. It links to the catalog and reports the actual publisher mode.\n- `kotobase.net` is the storage and retrieval plane for immutable blocks and addressable data.\n- `itonami.cloud` is the agent-work plane.\n- `murakumo.cloud` is the compute plane, including GPU capacity.\n\n## Current truth boundary\n\nThe current implemented publication path is local signed identity plus IPNS. A hosted Passkey publisher on `kotoba.cloud` is not live and must be advertised as false until the ceremony, authorization, receipt, and recovery path are deployed and observed. SourceCID, BuildCID, ArtifactCID, semantic definition CID, release-head CID, and mutable aliases remain different identifiers.\n\n## User path\n\n`inspect -> authorize -> store immutable blocks -> advance signed name -> discover in catalog -> operate through cloud controls`. Web pages explain and verify this path; they do not replace the CLI operation or invent another authority."}]
